ARCHIVE SUMMARY — THIRD SHINOBI WORLD WAR
Konohagakure Historical Records

The Third Shinobi World War saw fierce fighting between Konoha and its
rivals, including Iwagakure of the Land of Earth. Konoha suffered heavy
losses but produced legendary heroes.

Konoha Highlights:
- Minato Namikaze, later the Fourth Hokage, earned worldwide fame as "The
  Yellow Flash" for the Flying Thunder God Technique. Iwa forces were
  issued flee-on-sight orders against him.
- Minato's single-handed defeat of a large enemy force at the Kannabi
  Bridge is credited with turning the tide.
- Team Minato — Kakashi Hatake, Obito Uchiha, and Rin Nohara — served in
  this war. Kakashi received his Sharingan from his dying comrade Obito
  during the Kannabi Bridge mission.

Outcome: The war ended with a treaty. It forged the reputation of the
Fourth Hokage and shaped a generation of the village's leadership.
